        <div class="founder__text">
            <p>For three years, I’ve lived on the ground side of wellness travel, building packages, holding logistics together, making sure every piece of a healing holiday actually fits. Along the way I’ve seen how easily a beautiful trip is promised, and how gently it can unravel in the details, a practitioner double booked, transport that doesn’t quite sync, timing that rushes the very stillness someone came searching for. It’s rarely a lack of care. It’s just that no one stitched the pieces together with enough Tenderness.</p>
            <p>MĀRGHĀ is where I get to do that stitching. My own quiet path to a calmer, healthier self has taught me what true restoration feels like, not just relaxed, but brought gently back to yourself. That’s the journey I love building: one held softly enough to simply let go, breathe, and Receive.</p>
            <p class="founder__sig founder__sig--sans"><strong>-Senumi Evni,</strong> <em>Co-Founder</em></p>
